      "writtenOn": "2025-10-27T21:12:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, right.  I don\u0027t know why I did this.  Hmm... I guess forcing callers to explicitly pass `\u0026status_` makes it clearer that the call may mutate `status_`.  But this line of argumentation also applies to all the other things mutated by `ReadMoreData` (e.g. `codec_memory_`) so maybe let\u0027s just indeed simplify and avoid this out param.\n\nInterestingly, when `PngReadMoreData` returns `false`/failure, then `ProgressiveDecoder::PngContinueDecode` immediately sets `status_` to `kError`.  So setting `status_` inside `ReadMoreData` is kind of unnecessary.\n\nDone (applied the suggestion).  I am not sure if we want any other follow-ups.  Probably not in this CL?",
